<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech fund IPF KB posts 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Czech fund IPF KB posts 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech fund IPF Komercni Banky a.s., managed by a unit of the country's largest commercial bank, Komercni Banka, said it had a 1.937 billion crown loss for 1996, after a 15.7 million profit in 1995.</p>
<p>Results for year ending December 31, 1995: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net result			  1,937.11 loss vs    15.64 profit</p>
<p> Operating result		    270.98 loss vs   205.10 loss</p>
<p>Result from financial</p>
<p> operations, including tax     1,666.13 loss vs   220.74 profit</p>
<p> Total assets		     10,529.37	vs 9,689.11</p>
<p>Note. The fund's shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange. The fund is managed by Komercni's investment arm, IKS KB.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
